  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "tag": "System design",
      "heading": "How do you deliver a report that takes *5 minutes*?",
      "narration": "Your report takes five minutes to generate. If the user waits on the same connection, they get a 504 error. So how do you deliver it? Like a restaurant.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "text": "Request",
          "icon": "client",
          "at": "Your report takes"
        },
        {
          "text": "5 min",
          "icon": "scheduler",
          "at": "five minutes",
          "sfx": "clock"
        },
        {
          "text": "504",
          "at": "a 504 error"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "at": "how do you deliver"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Asynchronous",
      "narration": "They take your order, give you a number, and call you when it's ready. That's asynchronous. The API answers right away with a 202 and a job ID: your order number.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "They take your order",
          "show": [
            "frontend",
            "api"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "frontend",
            "to": "api",
            "label": "GET /report",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "That's asynchronous",
          "note": {
            "text": "*Async*: you don't wait on the line",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "answers right away",
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "frontend",
            "label": "202 + jobId",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "frontend": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "your order number",
          "note": {
            "text": "jobId = *your order number*",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "The queue",
      "narration": "The request goes into a queue: a list of pending jobs. It survives even if your server restarts, and if lots of requests arrive, they wait in line instead of taking the API down.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "goes into a queue",
          "show": [
            "queue"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "queue",
            "label": "job #8f2a",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "status": {
            "queue": "busy",
            "frontend": "idle"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "pending jobs",
          "focus": [
            "queue"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "Queue = *a list of pending jobs*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "server restarts",
          "note": {
            "text": "Survives *restarts*",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "wait in line",
          "focus": [
            "api",
            "queue"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "Lots of requests → *they wait in line*",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "The worker",
      "narration": "A worker, another program in your backend, takes the job, reads the sales from the database and saves the file to S3. However long it takes, nobody waits.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "A worker",
          "show": [
            "worker"
          ],
          "focus": [
            "worker"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "takes the job",
          "packet": {
            "from": "queue",
            "to": "worker",
            "label": "job #8f2a",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "status": {
            "queue": "idle",
            "worker": "busy"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "reads the sales",
          "packet": {
            "from": "worker",
            "to": "db",
            "label": "query"
          },
          "status": {
            "db": "busy"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "saves the file",
          "packet": {
            "from": "worker",
            "to": "store",
            "label": "report.csv",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "db": "idle",
            "worker": "ok",
            "store": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "nobody waits",
          "focus": [],
          "camera": [],
          "note": {
            "text": "However long it takes: *nobody waits*",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "How you find out",
      "narration": "And the user finds out because the frontend asks every few seconds if it's ready, that's polling, or because the server tells it with SSE. Then they download it.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "asks every few seconds",
          "packet": {
            "from": "frontend",
            "to": "api",
            "label": "ready yet?",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "that's polling",
          "note": {
            "text": "*Polling*: asking every few seconds",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "server tells it",
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "frontend",
            "label": "ready!",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "sfx": "notify",
          "note": {
            "text": "*SSE*: the server tells you",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "download it",
          "packet": {
            "from": "store",
            "to": "frontend",
            "label": "download",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "frontend": "ok"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "Order, number, call",
      "narration": "Order, number, call: that's how you deliver slow work. Would you use polling or SSE? The full video is on the channel.",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Answer *202 + ID* right away",
          "at": "Order, number"
        },
        {
          "text": "*Queue + worker* do the heavy work",
          "at": "deliver slow work"
        },
        {
          "text": "Notify with *polling or SSE*",
          "at": "Would you use"
        }
      ],
      "cta": "Full video on the channel ▶"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Common queues: SQS, RabbitMQ, Redis (BullMQ, Sidekiq), or Kafka if you already run it. For something simple, a jobs table in the database also works.",
    "A background thread inside the API loses the job if the process restarts and competes for CPU with requests; the queue separates the two.",
    "Polling is the simplest and works behind any proxy; SSE avoids empty checks; WebSocket is two-way and isn't needed here.",
    "S3 (or any object storage) serves the file directly, usually through a signed URL that expires."
  ],
  "publish": {
    "titles": [
      "How Do You Deliver a Report That Takes 5 Minutes? (Queue + Worker)",
      "Async Explained With a Restaurant"
    ],
    "description": "If something takes minutes, don't make the user wait on the same connection: 202 + a job ID, a queue, a worker and a notification.",
    "extra": [
      "🎬 The full video (from a simple API to a queue, a worker and a cron job) is on the channel."
    ],
    "comment": "Polling or SSE? Which would you use?",
